  "generated_description": "<div class=\"mountain-description prose prose-stone max-w-none\">\n  <p><strong>Danville Mountain</strong> is a 1,122-foot summit in New Jersey. The Danville Mountain Trail covers 8.3 miles with about 92 feet of elevation gain \u2014 a gradual walk with modest climbing.</p>\n  <h3>Getting There</h3><p>The trailhead is at <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=40.94571,-74.8055\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">40.94571, -74.8055</a> (tap for driving directions). It's roughly 70 miles north of Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. Arrive early on weekends \u2014 trailhead lots at popular peaks fill quickly, and cell service is often unreliable once you leave the highway.</p>\n  <h3>When to Go</h3><p>Spring through fall is the main season. Conditions change fast in the shoulder months \u2014 check a point forecast for the summit, not the nearest town, before you commit.</p>\n  <h3>Know Before You Go</h3><p>Most hikers should budget about 3.0 hours of moving time; add margin for breaks, photos and the descent. Download the GPX track from this page before you go \u2014 cell coverage is unreliable in the mountains and a saved route works offline in any GPS app. Conditions change: verify current access, closures and weather with the official land manager before you go. Trail data is sourced from OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).</p>\n  <p>Looking to link objectives or plan a weekend? Nearby summits include Jenny Jump Mountain, Baldpate Mountain and Upper Pohatcong Mountain \u2014 each has its own guide on this site.</p>\n</div>",
